--- !u!114 &218105343
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 218105342}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8834251f23247d949a7310790cbd9e9d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimpleNPC
  firstTimeLines:
  - Alright, You better listen up here
  - The console questions are gonna be difficult starting from at this point.
  - Alright, Let's start with else - if! or if else
  - In an if-else statement, when the if condition is true,
  - "The else part doesn't evaluate to anything\u2014it just gets completely ignored...
    like me :("
  - The program runs the if block and jumps right past the else.
  - 'The else only wakes up when the if is false. So in that moment, the else is
    just sitting there, doing nothing. '
  - Thats that!
  - OH WAIT!
  - 'I FORGOT ABOUT '
  - ARRAYS!!
  - So basically ARRAYS... they're a fixed size row of boxes that all hold the same
    type.
  - Each box is numbered, starting from 0, so you grab stuff by its index.
  - Oh array index is just a label, it starts from zero to infinity
  - You can't add or remove boxes, but you can swap what's inside!
  repeatLines:
  - Quick Recap!
  - 'SO! when the IF is TRUE, the ELSE is completely ignored, it just sits there,
    doing nothing. That''s it!  '
  - Oh! Array a fixed size, numbered list of same type items. Change what's inside,
    not how many.... basically a storage.
  textSpeed: 0.001
  useTalkCounter: 1
  timesTalked: 0
